WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.267
Traffic sign detection requires reliable recognition of small

2
00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:07.933
objects under variations in scale,

3
00:00:07.933 --> 00:00:09.900
visibility, and illumination.

4
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:15.767
SMDDFNet addresses this representation problem by integrating

5
00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:20.033
spatial attention and adaptive frequency filtering within a state

6
00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:21.433
space detection architecture.

7
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:29.433
At long range, a sign may contain very few informative pixels.

8
00:00:29.433 --> 00:00:32.467
Occlusion and changing illumination further reduce the

9
00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:34.433
reliability of its visual features.

10
00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:38.967
An effective representation must preserve local structure while

11
00:00:38.967 --> 00:00:41.500
incorporating context from the surrounding scene.

12
00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:48.333
The model processes a square input image with a resolution of six

13
00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:52.133
hundred and forty pixels. A hierarchical state space backbone

14
00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:54.567
extracts progressively deeper features.

15
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.200
Dynamic Dual Fusion operates on the deepest representation.

16
00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.667
A feature aggregation neck then produces three resolutions for

17
00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:03.533
object detection.

18
00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:08.967
The backbone follows the Mamba YOLO design,

19
00:01:08.967 --> 00:01:12.067
combining a convolutional stem, spatial merging,

20
00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:13.800
and visual state space blocks.

21
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.867
In the B configuration, spatial dimensions decrease across four

22
00:01:17.867 --> 00:01:21.800
stages, while channel capacity increases from sixty four to five

23
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:22.600
hundred and twelve.

24
00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:29.233
Selective scanning propagates a hidden state across spatial

25
00:01:29.233 --> 00:01:32.867
positions. This allows the representation at one location to

26
00:01:32.867 --> 00:01:35.300
incorporate information from more distant regions.

27
00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:40.167
The scan computation scales linearly with sequence length.

28
00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.467
This property applies to the scan operation,

29
00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:45.467
rather than every operation in the complete detector.

30
00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:52.067
The spatial branch applies Efficient Multi Scale Attention to

31
00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:55.700
grouped features. Pooling along height and width captures

32
00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:59.933
directional structure alongside a local convolutional response.

33
00:02:00.733 --> 00:02:04.600
Cross branch interactions generate a sigmoid attention map,

34
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.833
which reweights the original grouped features.

35
00:02:09.867 --> 00:02:12.867
The frequency branch first expands the channel dimension,

36
00:02:12.867 --> 00:02:15.967
then applies a real Fourier transform to the spatial features.

37
00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:20.300
A learned complex filter modulates the resulting spectrum.

38
00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:24.167
The inverse transform and channel projection return this response

39
00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:25.800
to the spatial representation.

40
00:02:28.833 --> 00:02:33.133
The dynamic filter is assembled from four learned complex filter

41
00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:38.167
bases. Global average pooling summarizes the input for a routing

42
00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:38.733
network.

43
00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.967
A softmax produces a separate mixture for each expanded channel.

44
00:02:43.967 --> 00:02:47.267
The effective frequency response therefore adapts to the current

45
00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:47.867
input.

46
00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:53.800
Both branches receive the complete input tensor.

47
00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.267
Their projected outputs are concatenated,

48
00:02:56.267 --> 00:03:00.433
then processed by two successive stages of parallel three by

49
00:03:00.433 --> 00:03:03.467
three and five by five convolutions.

50
00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:08.333
The second stage responses are multiplied element by element.

51
00:03:08.333 --> 00:03:11.600
Independently projected branch features provide additive paths

52
00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.567
before the final output convolution.

53
00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:20.433
The neck combines top down and bottom up aggregation.

54
00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:26.133
Upsampling, concatenation, and XSS blocks connect representations

55
00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:28.500
at different spatial resolutions.

56
00:03:29.233 --> 00:03:32.300
Prediction features are produced at strides of eight,

57
00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:35.733
sixteen, and thirty two pixels, supporting detection across

58
00:03:35.733 --> 00:03:36.800
object scales.

59
00:03:39.633 --> 00:03:43.133
Each head predicts class scores and discrete distributions for

60
00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:47.067
bounding box distances. Decoding converts these distributions

61
00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:48.900
into candidate box coordinates.

62
00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:53.433
Confidence thresholding removes low scoring candidates.

63
00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:57.933
Non maximum suppression reduces overlapping detections associated

64
00:03:57.933 --> 00:03:59.400
with the same object.

65
00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:06.000
The manuscript images show representative visual challenges:

66
00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.200
small targets, partial occlusion,

67
00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:12.333
and difficult illumination. The original annotations identify the

68
00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:13.433
regions of interest.

69
00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.067
These selected examples illustrate the task.

70
00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:20.400
Dataset level conclusions must be established separately through

71
00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.433
complete and consistent evaluation.

72
00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:28.500
The architectural contribution centers on dual domain

73
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:32.067
integration: spatial attention, input dependent frequency

74
00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:36.233
filtering, and multiplicative interactions between convolutional

75
00:04:36.233 --> 00:04:36.900
responses.

76
00:04:37.633 --> 00:04:40.767
The backbone and neck build on established designs.

77
00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:43.833
Controlled ablation experiments are required to quantify the

78
00:04:43.833 --> 00:04:46.033
contribution of each added component.

79
00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:51.567
The resulting architecture connects local evidence,

80
00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:55.533
spatial context, and adaptive filtering through a shared

81
00:04:55.533 --> 00:04:56.633
detection pipeline.

82
00:04:57.767 --> 00:05:02.367
SMDDFNet combines these complementary representations for traffic

83
00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:03.333
sign detection.